# VVDN -- 1 synthetic aircraft, REVERSE of VDN601 (from
# VVDN_DOTEN_3ACFT_TROMBONE_ILSV35L.scn): pushback from real Gate 26, taxi
# out, stop ~5s lined up on RWY 35R, takeoff roll, then real SID BUNTA 2G.
# Callsign VDN701 is SYNTHETIC (not a real ADS-B flight).
#
# v5 -- pushback leg updated per latest request: nose heading 263 deg (real
# bearing from Gate 26 to the new pushback-complete point computes to
# 261.1 deg -- close match) to 16.0524,108.2005 (was 16.0531,108.2005;
# shorter pushback, 159m instead of 380m). Downstream bearing from this new
# point to the next taxi point (16.0297,108.2038) is still ~172.0 deg, so
# the rest of the ground route is unaffected.
#
# ON THE REQUESTED 2KT PUSHBACK SPEED: still not usable, for the same
# reason as before (see below) -- 2kt = 1.03 m/s falls inside BlueSky's
# 0.1-2.0 m/s CAS/Mach ambiguity band, so it would still be misread as
# Mach ~1.0 (~680kt). Kept at the 4kt floor established in v4.
#
# v4 REBUILD -- 3 earlier attempts (ADDWPT/LNAV/VNAV; a HDG/SPD/ATDIST
# hybrid; then a first MOVE-only version) ALL still rocketed to ~650-680kt
# while still at the gate. Root-caused this time, for real: BlueSky's own
# CAS/Mach speed-ambiguity heuristic (bluesky/tools/aero.py, vcasormach()):
#   ismach = 0.1 < spd < casmach_thr        # casmach_thr = 2.0 m/s by default
# ANY nonzero commanded speed under 2.0 m/s (~3.9kt) -- e.g. the 2kt pushback
# / 3kt slow-taxi speeds this scenario originally used -- gets silently
# reinterpreted as a MACH NUMBER instead of calibrated airspeed. Mach 1.03
# at sea level IS ~680kt, which is exactly the bogus speed observed. This
# is a real, reproducible engine limitation (confirmed live with a bare
# single CRE/MOVE line and nothing else in the scenario), not a scripting
# mistake in the route/waypoints themselves.
# FIX: every commanded speed in this file is now either EXACTLY 0 (a true
# stop; 0 doesn't satisfy "spd > 0.1" so it's never misread) or >= 4kt,
# safely above the 3.9kt danger line.
# Also: this file uses plain MOVE commands (direct lat/lon/alt/hdg/spd
# assignment every few seconds), not BlueSky's ADDWPT/LNAV/VNAV/route
# engine -- the same mechanism already verified reliable in this session
# for HVN132_G4_ARR_REAL.scn / HVN132_G6_ARR_REAL.scn (real ADS-B replays)
# and the pre-existing vag672_adsb_replay.scn. Every position/altitude/
# speed below was computed by this session (not hand-typed) via straight-
# line interpolation between the named real points/altitudes/speeds
# established earlier (see below), sampled every ~3s on the ground and
# ~25s once airborne. Since this is fully scripted rather than driven by
# BlueSky's own performance model, the acceleration/climb profile is a
# reasonable physical approximation (constant-acceleration-equivalent
# takeoff roll, linear climb rate per leg), NOT the aircraft's real thrust/
# drag envelope -- the tradeoff for reliability after 3 autopilot-driven
# attempts each failed live testing.
#
# NOTE ON "GATE 26": VDN601 in the reference file actually parks at real
# Gate 24 (16.05337,108.20189, per its own last ADDWPT and gates.geojson),
# not Gate 26 -- flagged honestly, since this file follows the gate
# explicitly named in this request.
#
# GROUND ROUTE -- every point cross-checked against the real taxiway
# centerlines in FTS Server/data/aerodrome_layout/datasets/vietnam_kml_layout/
# normalized/airports/VVDN/taxiway_centerlines.geojson (all within ~3-25m of
# a real centerline vertex -- within this dataset's own granularity):
#  - Start point = real Gate 26 stand, 16.05262199,108.2019728 (gates.geojson).
#  - Pushback-complete point 16.0524,108.2005 (real bearing 261.1 deg from
#    Gate 26 -- close match to the requested 263 deg).
#  - Hold-heading-172 taxi to 16.0297,108.2038 (real bearing 172.0 deg,
#    matches the requested heading almost exactly).
#  - Turn right to 16.0292,108.2029 (real bearing 240 deg from the exit
#    point -- a real right turn from 172).
#  - Turn right to 16.0295,108.2026 (real bearing 316 deg -- again a real
#    right turn).
#  - Stop ~5s on RWY 35R at 16.0300,108.2024, ~108m north of the real RWY
#    35R threshold (16.02904,108.20253, runway_centerlines.geojson
#    "17L/35R"). Bearing into this point (339 deg) is already close to the
#    352 deg runway heading used for the takeoff roll.
#  - Real RWY 17L/35R centerline: 108.19800,16.06037 (17L end) <->
#    108.20253,16.02904 (35R end/threshold), length ~1.90NM.
#
# TAKEOFF ROLL / LIFTOFF POINT (16.062960,108.197580): NOT charted -- derived
# the same way BlueSky's own internal "ADDWPT TAKEOFF" special case does
# (route.py's addwptStack(): rwydist=2.0NM along the runway heading from the
# lineup point). Speed ramps 0->170kt as sqrt(distance) (constant-
# deceleration-equivalent physics -- already safely above the 4kt floor
# from the very first sample, since the sqrt curve rises steeply at first).
# Altitude stays 0 until the last 40% of the roll then climbs to 500ft,
# approximating a realistic late rotation/liftoff point.
#
# CLIMB-OUT / SID -- real AIP Vietnam "STANDARD DEPARTURE CHART - INSTRUMENT
# (SID) - ICAO, DA NANG/DA NANG INTL (VVDN), RNAV RWY 35L/R" (AD 2-VVDN-9-6,
# AMDT 01/23), BUNTA 2G DEPARTURE tabular description:
#   010 CF DN456  crs 360(359T)            alt -2450m(8038ft)
#   020 TF HOKIN   crs 074(072.5T) 43.23km  alt -FL110(11000ft)
#   030 TF BINKU   crs 075(074.0T) 43.79km  alt (none charted)
#   040 TF BUNTA   crs 057(056.0T) 54.24km  alt (none charted)
# Waypoint coordinates from the same chart's own WGS-84 list:
#   DN456 16'20'03"N 108'11'33"E, HOKIN 16'27'04"N 108'34'43"E,
#   BINKU 16'33'35"N 108'58'23"E, BUNTA 16'50'00"N 109'23'42"E.
# BINKU/BUNTA carry no altitude restriction on the real chart, and the
# BUNTA 2G table has no speed-limit column at all -- their altitudes
# (19000ft/24000ft) and every climb speed below are a reasonable assumed
# continued-climb schedule (250kt below 10,000ft, accelerating above),
# flagged honestly as NOT charted numbers (unlike DN456/HOKIN's real
# altitudes and all 4 waypoints' real courses/distances/coordinates, which
# are). Straight-line MOVE interpolation between these named points means
# heading changes in discrete jumps at each waypoint rather than a smoothed
# turn -- a known simplification of the MOVE-replay approach.
#
# PERFORMANCE MODEL -- user asked for BADA specifically. Earlier this
# session BADA looked unusable (bluesky/resources/performance/BADA/ only
# had a placeholder README, no licensed data, and "PERF BADA" failed live).
# On follow-up, found the REAL BADA data (B738__.OPF/.APF, ReleaseSummary,
# SYNONYM.NEW, BADA v3.16) was already present elsewhere in this repo, at
# bluesky/data/performance/bada/ -- just not in the path BlueSky's own
# coeff_bada.check()/init() actually reads from. Copied those 4 files into
# bluesky/resources/performance/BADA/ (the gitignored dir the engine
# expects; confirmed via .gitignore this is exactly the intended drop-in
# location) and re-verified live: "PERF BADA" now succeeds ("Selected BADA
# as performance model", 1832 aircraft entries / B738 coefficient set
# loaded). NOTE: this file itself still doesn't use it -- it was rebuilt as
# a pure MOVE replay (no autopilot/performance system involved at all)
# after 3 ADDWPT/LNAV/VNAV-based attempts each rocketed to ~650-680kt from
# an unrelated engine bug (see above). BADA is now available for scenarios
# that actually drive aircraft through the autopilot/route system.

00:00:00.00>TRAILS ON
00:00:00.00>ASAS ON

# ============ VDN701 -- pushback from real Gate 26, taxi, RWY 35R, BUNTA 2G ============

00:00:00.00>CRE VDN701,B738,16.052622,108.201973,263,0,0
00:00:00.50>MOVE VDN701,16.052622,108.201973,0,263,4.0
